Characteristics of Population
1. Complete Set

A population contains all observations of interest.

2. Parameter

A parameter is a numerical value that summarizes the entire population.

Examples:

Population Mean (μ)
Population Variance (σ²)
Examples of Population
1. Population in a School Study
All students enrolled in a school.
Used to determine the average score of all students.
2. Population in Market ResearchZ*
All consumers in a city.
Used to understand purchasing behaviour.
3. Population in a Medical Study
All patients with a specific disease.
Used to study the effectiveness of a drug.
Characteristics of Sample Data
1. Subset

A sample represents only a portion of the population.

2. Statistic

A statistic is a numerical value summarizing sample data.

Examples:

Sample Mean
Sample Variance
3. Random Sampling

Samples should be selected randomly to avoid bias.Examples of Sample
1. School Study
Sample: A group of 50 students from the school.
Use Case: Estimate the average marks of all students using the sample mean.
2. Market Research
Sample: 500 consumers from a city.
Purpose: Estimate the purchasing behaviour of the entire population.
3. Medical Study
Sample: 200 patients.
Purpose: Test the effectiveness of a drug.
